138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (We also ensure our staff remain connected to the wider RAFAC. Attendance at the Wing Conference allows us to align our training approach with the broader vision, while still maintaining the high standards we set at squadron level.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
139 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Sporting Success and Milestones)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
140 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Under the leadership of our Sports Officer, CI Stone, we have engaged in a number of external sporting events. A particular highlight was our Junior team winning the Wing 5-a-side competition and progressing to the regional level, a fantastic achievement.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (We also celebrated the passing out parade of Intake 02/25. These parades, introduced a number of years ago, mark the completion of initial training and showcase the remarkable development cadets achieve in just six months.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (With family and friends in attendance, and an inspiring address from our reviewing officer, Lt Col Glyn Potts MBE \(Army Cadet Force\), the event was a proud moment for all involved.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Delivering Excellence in Training)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (Behind the scenes, the level of training delivered at 317 is significant. Our team includes seven Method of Instruction \(MOI\) qualified instructors, two qualified teachers, and a strong system of continuous development and quality assurance.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 52 0 R
/E (This ensures that both staff and cadet NCOs are actively involved in delivering our monthly training programme, maintaining consistently high standards across all activities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
